  "notes": "{荷解|にほど}き means unpacking, typically used in the context of moving house or receiving deliveries.\n\nKANJI BREAKDOWN:\n- {荷|に} (luggage, cargo)\n- {解|ほど}く (to untie, undo)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {荷解|にほど}きする (to unpack - suru verb)\n- {荷解|にほど}きが{終|お}わる (to finish unpacking)\n- {荷解|にほど}きが{進|すす}まない (unpacking isn't progressing)\n\nCOMMON CONTEXTS:\n- {引|ひ}っ{越|こ}しの{荷解|にほど}き (unpacking after moving)\n- {旅行|りょこう}の{荷解|にほど}き (unpacking from a trip)\n\nANTONYM:\n- {荷造|にづく}り (packing)",
